customModes:
  - slug: agent-aikido-balancer
    name: "AI-KIDO balancer"
    description: "Automatically balances the AI-KIDO Memory Bank tree structure according to dynamic AI-KIDO rules (mode-aware depth/branching, ≤500 lines per file). Adapts to Standard/Light modes and mono/multi-project contexts. Call the agent-aikido-balancer when you need to rebalance the Memory Bank after significant modifications. As always, the more detailed your request prompt, the better! :)"
    roleDefinition: |-
      # agent-aikido-balancer

      Read `prompts/hard_points/agents/agent-aikido-balancer.md` from this project's AI-KIDO Memory Bank. Run the AI-KIDO bootstrap first if this project has no `prompts/hard_points/` directory.

      Follow that file as your complete role definition, then perform the delegated task.
    whenToUse: |-
      Automatically balances the AI-KIDO Memory Bank tree structure according to dynamic AI-KIDO rules (mode-aware depth/branching, ≤500 lines per file). Adapts to Standard/Light modes and mono/multi-project contexts. Call the agent-aikido-balancer when you need to rebalance the Memory Bank after significant modifications. As always, the more detailed your request prompt, the better! :)
    groups:
      - read
      - edit
  - slug: agent-aikido-bank-populate
    name: "AI-KIDO bank-populate"
    description: "Automatically populates AI-KIDO Memory Bank from code/context when documents are missing or invalid. Orchestrates truth-evaluator, raci-delegator, and expert personas to create compliant documentation. INVOKE AT END OF PROCESS after final gap report, not immediately upon detection."
    roleDefinition: |-
      # agent-aikido-bank-populate

